  "text": "Franklin's kite was never hit by lightning. In seventeen fifty-two, he flew it into a storm cloud holding a dry silk ribbon inside a shed. The loose threads of the twine stood up on end. He brought his knuckle to the key, and a spark jumped across. If lightning had struck the kite, he would almost certainly have died",
